# XGS PON Core Development Principles

> **Reference**: http://wiki/moin/action/show/RnD0045%3A%20C%20Coding%20Standard
> **Applies to**: All XGS PON project code
> **Maintainer**: frzhou
> **Version**: 1.0

---

## 1. Code Style Consistency

### 1.1 Preserve Existing Style
- **MANDATORY**: Read surrounding code before making changes to maintain consistent style
- Do not arbitrarily change indentation, spacing, brace placement, or other formatting
- Follow existing naming conventions in the file (snake_case, camelCase, etc.)
- Preserve the existing code organization structure

### 1.2 Style Detection Method
Before modifying a file, observe the following elements:
- Indentation: spaces or tabs, how many characters
- Braces: same line as if/for or next line
- Variable naming: prefix rules, casing rules
- Function naming: module prefix rules
- Comment style: single-line / multi-line / Doxygen format

### 1.3 Whitespace Rules
- **Blank lines must be truly empty** - no spaces or tabs
- No trailing whitespace at end of lines
- Keep one newline at end of file
